James inquired about changing colors in a raster image within Adobe Illustrator. I provided a step-by-step guide that included using the "Image Trace" feature for conversion to vector, editing colors via the "Recolor Artwork" option, or using color adjustment effects directly on the raster image. He later asked where to adjust settings for Image Trace, and I detailed accessing the Image Trace panel and setting options like Threshold, Paths, and Noise. Finally, James reported issues with color changes affecting the entire traced image. I guided him through ungrouping the image, selecting specific components, and using the Color panel or "Recolor Artwork" feature to change individual colors effectively.
